<h2>A Sample Weekly Plan Built Around an Under Desk Elliptical</h2>
<p>This plan uses the elliptical for both light activity and part of your 150 moderate minutes, and adds what it misses.</p>
<div class="table-wrap"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Day</th><th>At your desk</th><th>Away from your desk</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Monday</td><td>Light pedaling in blocks + one 20-min moderate block</td><td>20-min strength routine (squats, push-ups, rows)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Tuesday</td><td>Light pedaling + 15-min interval session</td><td>15-min walk</td></tr>
<tr><td>Wednesday</td><td>Light pedaling + one 20-min moderate block</td><td>20-min strength routine</td></tr>
<tr><td>Thursday</td><td>Light pedaling + 15-min interval session</td><td>15-min walk</td></tr>
<tr><td>Friday</td><td>Light pedaling + one 20-min moderate block</td><td>Longer walk or bike ride</td></tr>
<tr><td>Weekend</td><td>Optional</td><td>Active hobby, longer walk, balance work</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<p>The desk blocks alone give you about 90 moderate minutes a week. The walks make up the rest of the 150, and the two strength sessions cover the muscle-strengthening guideline. If you are just starting, halve the moderate blocks for the first two weeks.</p>

<h2>Best Machines for Moderate-Intensity Sessions</h2>
<p>To reach moderate effort, you need enough resistance and a machine that stays put when you push. Based on specs and owner reviews:</p>
