[[product:lifepro-flexstride|3]]
[[compare:cubii-jr2,deskcycle-ellipse,lifepro-flexstride,cubii-jr2-plus]]
<p>A motorized machine is a poor choice if exercise is your goal, since passive mode keeps you in the light zone. If you are unsure which type to buy, our comparison of <a href="/do-under-desk-elliptical-machines/">manual vs motorized under desk elliptical machines</a> breaks it down, and our <a href="/does-under-desk-elliptical-work/">goal-by-goal results guide</a> shows what to expect.</p>

<h2>The Verdict: Is an Under Desk Elliptical Good Exercise?</h2>
<p>Yes, with a condition. At an easy pace it is good light activity that makes a desk day less sedentary. At a brisk pace with resistance, judged by the talk test, it is genuine moderate exercise that counts toward your 150 minutes. It will not cover strength, balance or bone health, so pair it with walking and a couple of short strength sessions each week.</p>
<p>If you want a machine with enough resistance to make your desk time count, start with the [[amazon:cubii-jr2|Cubii JR2]].</p>
